  "details": "This is probably one of the last things VRChat needs so far, but the mic icon is pretty annoying (as well as multiple in-game notifications). Of course, as it was suggested by other users, separating notifications and the voice indicator should be possible, but I'm making a slightly different request here. \n\nI suggest replacing the regular mic icon with other UI elements in the middle of the screen (for example, a waveform responding to the user's voice). People often forget or don't bother about disabling their UI, which is a bit annoying when they record a video or take screenshots with it, so at least it would look better if for some reason they leave it on. \n\nAnd that's just one tiny detail about the UI. Notifications could use more space than just the bottom left corner. Overall, in order to present my vision of what good UI could look like in VRChat, I made this rough example below.\n\nNote: the waveform is just an idea. Personally, I would prefer it since I talk very rarely, but, again, it's just an option. Perhaps an icon would be nice too.",
